b) Use the Software, its source code, or derivative works for commercial purposes, service bureau operations, or as a Software as a Service (SaaS) offering;
c) Create derivative works, adapt, translate, decompile, reverse engineer, or attempt to extract the underlying logic of the Software;
d) Sublicense, rent, sell, transfer, or assign any rights in the Software under any legal title;
e) Use the source code, architecture, documentation, or prompts to train, fine-tune, or feed artificial intelligence models or autonomous agents without prior written permission.

The public availability of the source code in remote version control repositories (such as GitHub) is solely for documentary, prior-art verification, and technical portfolio demonstration purposes. It does NOT constitute a waiver of economic rights, nor does it grant any public license for use, modification, or redistribution.

